Rule 3 (out, if provided, must have the same shape as input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_2) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀ i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 4 (all input dimensions are non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀ i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 5 (complex input preserves complex precision in out)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 9 then dtype_(v_2) = 9 else if dtype_(v_1) = 10 then dtype_(v_2) = 10
